# Hyundai i10 second generation five-door, 2014-2020.
#
# The IA i10: the European-built city car with the tall body, the hexagonal
# grille and the rising beltline. UK sales from 30 January 2014.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyundai_i10
#
# Dimensions 3.645 x 1.660 x 1.500 m, wheelbase 2.385 m. The Autocar launch
# story gives 3,665 mm length; 3.645 is used and the discrepancy is recorded.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is side-on but elevated, not a true level profile;
# the front and rear three-quarters show the lamps and tail. The flank is
# estimated; the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Hyundai UK chart was found. White, grey, blue and red
# are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 65/428, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 65. Classes 0,1.
# Dates are road presence: 2014 intro, retires staggered 2033-2036.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/hyundai-i10-mk2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/hyundai-i10-mk2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/hyundai-i10-mk2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the flank is estimated, image 1 being side-on but
# elevated rather than a level profile. Length 3.645 m is used, not Autocar's
# 3.665 m. Pre-facelift fascia; the headlamp and rear-lamp curvature and the
# door surfacing are simplified.


obj=citycar
name=HyundaiI10Mk2(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2014
intro_month=1
retire_year=2036
retire_month=6
speed=160
length=2
class=0,1
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=428

